<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Quemuenchatocha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1539</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Quemuenchatocha was the zaque, ruler of the northern Muisca at Hunza (modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunja">Tunja</a>), when the Spanish arrived. In 1537 the conquistador <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gonzalo-jimenez-de-quesada">Gonzalo Jiménez de Quesada</a> seized Hunza, captured the aged ruler and plundered his treasure. He died soon after in captivity, and his successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aquiminzaque">Aquiminzaque</a> was executed in 1540.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/quemuenchatocha.jpg" alt="Quemuenchatocha" width="143" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:QUEMUENCHATOCHA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
